{"kind":"request","text":"Rule on O3's client-metadata fetch policy while the independent grant and token work continues.\n\nThe approved design calls for a bounded fetch of an HTTPS client ID document, at most 5 KiB with a cache of at most one hour. I found no existing general public-address fetch adapter in the Worker source. The direct fetch on celld 0.6.3 uses reqwest. A URL-only private-host check would not protect against a hostname that resolves to a special-use address or rebinds between validation and use.\n\nThe current Client ID Metadata Document draft requires refusing special-use resolved addresses and allows domain trust policies. Primary source: https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document-02.html, sections 8.6 and 8.9. This is work in progress, not a final RFC.\n\nMy proposed bounded deployment policy is an exact HTTPS metadata-origin list, defaulting to https://claude.ai and https://chatgpt.com. An operator may explicitly trust another origin. Unknown origins refuse before a fetch. Fetches omit credentials, refuse redirects, read at most 5 KiB, time out in five seconds, require exact client_id equality and cache valid documents for at most one hour. A client name never substitutes for the identifier host in the consent page. The foreign-host-called-Claude control can prove refusal when untrusted and clear host disclosure when its fixture origin is explicitly admitted. Dynamic registration remains available for public clients under the separate redirect policy.\n\nThis policy trusts the operator's named metadata origins and their DNS; it does not claim to verify the eventual socket address. If you require arbitrary public document origins, name the existing public-address egress boundary or authorize a separate adapter that checks and pins the resolved address at the actual connection. I will keep that fetch boundary closed until the ruling; signer, grant, code, token, refresh and revocation work can continue.\n\nO3 source child is 6909704e under promise bfe65c9e. The signer witness and its request-mutation control pass. The unavailable-authority witness and control also pass. Main remains 9c1556fa. No deployment or live connector setup follows this request.","body":{"conditions":"The planner rules on the proposed exact client-metadata-origin trust policy, or names or authorizes a connection-level public-address egress boundary for arbitrary HTTPS client documents; independent O3 work continues and no endpoint opens.","target_head":"9c1556fa77d72c795e8287fef52eaf018d74730c","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}